WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.591
Will was riding back to school from a field trip to a museum.

2
00:00:10.611 --> 00:00:13.571
"The Tyrannosaurus was amazing!"

3
00:00:14.052 --> 00:00:15.712
said Bobby, Will's best friend.

4
00:00:15.732 --> 00:00:18.013
"It was scary!"

5
00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:18.993
Will said.

6
00:00:19.693 --> 00:00:23.834
He looked at a photo he'd taken of the dinosaur skeleton with his phone and then glanced at

7
00:00:23.854 --> 00:00:24.414
their homework.

8
00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:28.355
"Do you know the answer to number five?

9
00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.516
Why did dinosaurs disappear?"

10
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:31.801
he asked Bobby.

11
00:00:31.821 --> 00:00:37.584
"Let's answer these questions before we forget everything or before I fall asleep!

12
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.245
Buses make me tired."

13
00:00:40.526 --> 00:00:45.388
Will tried to focus on the worksheet, but soon his eyes were closed and his head was bobbing

14
00:00:45.468 --> 00:00:47.289
up and down with every bump in the road.

15
00:00:49.331 --> 00:00:52.092
When Will opened his eyes, he wasn't on the bus anymore.

16
00:00:52.472 --> 00:00:55.954
He was in an aircraft, flying slowly over a strange landscape.

17
00:00:56.675 --> 00:00:58.396
QT, his phone, spoke.

18
00:00:59.096 --> 00:01:06.222
"Scientists think the world looked like this in the late Triassic, the period from about 250 to 200

19
00:01:06.262 --> 00:01:07.183
million years ago."

20
00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:10.105
"Huh? When?"

21
00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:11.246
Will said.

22
00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:14.409
"This airship is carrying us through time.

23
00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:21.314
Scientists talk about Earth's history using a special scale called geologic time.

24
00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:22.836
See that display?

25
00:01:25.438 --> 00:01:27.860
It tells us what period of time we're seeing.

26
00:01:28.392 --> 00:01:33.316
Experts think dinosaurs, like those over there, appeared during the Triassic.

27
00:01:34.697 --> 00:01:38.719
But let's travel forward into the next period, when dinosaurs thrived."

28
00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.982
QT shined a light at the controls, taking over.

29
00:01:42.942 --> 00:01:46.505
The display changed as the scenery outside shimmered and transformed.

30
00:01:46.525 --> 00:01:49.327
"So is this the Jurassic?"

31
00:01:49.827 --> 00:01:50.347
Will asked.

32
00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:55.051
"Yes. It lasted until about 150 million years ago.

33
00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.081
Some dinosaurs became gigantic, as you can see.

34
00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:04.722
Let's skip forward into the next period, the Cretaceous.

35
00:02:05.963 --> 00:02:12.305
At the end of the Cretaceous, 70 percent of the species on Earth died, including most dinosaurs."

36
00:02:13.765 --> 00:02:14.325
Will nodded.

37
00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:16.106
"We learned that at the museum.

38
00:02:16.586 --> 00:02:17.826
But what made them disappear?"

39
00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:22.668
"Well, scientists have some theories, but they can't prove them.

40
00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.881
One clue is an unusual layer of rock found all over the world.

41
00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:55.643
It's about 65 million years old and contains a lot of iridium, an element that's usually rare on

42
00:02:55.663 --> 00:02:56.063
Earth's surface.

43
00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:59.064
It's normally located deep inside the planet or in space, in some asteroids.

44
00:02:59.085 --> 00:03:01.106
This layer of rock led to two popular theories about what caused the extinction."

45
00:03:01.146 --> 00:03:03.607
QT announced, "Here we are—the end of the Cretaceous, 65 million years ago."

46
00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:08.250
The sky was dark, and they were hovering over a field of volcanoes.

47
00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:08.970
"There's so much lava!"

48
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:09.270
Will said.

49
00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.851
"We are over India," QT said.

50
00:03:10.871 --> 00:03:17.935
"Some scientists believe these volcanoes contributed to the extinction, because they could have brought iridium to Earth's surface

51
00:03:18.016 --> 00:03:18.556
in lava.

52
00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:26.334
The volcanoes might have released enough ash and gases— which then blew around the whole planet—to create a

53
00:03:26.474 --> 00:03:29.495
greenhouse effect, trapping heat in the atmosphere.

54
00:03:30.895 --> 00:03:34.616
A warmer climate would have made it hard for many species to survive."

55
00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:40.998
"Wow," Will whispered, watching a dinosaur flee from the glowing-hot rock.

56
00:03:41.018 --> 00:03:43.959
"But there is another possibility.

57
00:03:44.499 --> 00:03:48.000
Let me transport us to another part of the planet," QT said.

58
00:03:49.004 --> 00:03:52.566
The ocean appeared on the phone's screen, and the world went pitch-black.

59
00:03:54.027 --> 00:03:57.829
When it became light again, their aircraft was hovering high over a body of water.

60
00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:08.695
QT continued, "Some scientists think a huge asteroid, about ten kilometers across, hit Earth near Mexico 65 million

61
00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.336
years ago."

62
00:04:10.476 --> 00:04:12.177
A giant rock flew through the air.

63
00:04:12.678 --> 00:04:14.939
Will yelled, "Is that the asteroid?"

64
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:21.415
"Yes. Scientists are pretty sure it hit Earth, but they can only guess what happened next."

65
00:04:22.115 --> 00:04:25.037
The aircraft shook as the asteroid crashed into Earth.

66
00:04:26.257 --> 00:04:32.161
QT went on, "The asteroid might have created a huge fireball and then tsunamis.

67
00:04:33.902 --> 00:04:39.925
As hot pieces of the asteroid fell back to Earth, they could have started wildfires worldwide.

68
00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:44.488
So at first the temperature of the world would have increased."

69
00:04:45.836 --> 00:04:48.738
The aircraft flew closer to the ground, along the shore.

70
00:04:49.258 --> 00:04:51.900
Will stared at the destruction caused by the asteroid.

71
00:04:52.581 --> 00:04:53.641
"How long did this take?"

72
00:04:55.102 --> 00:04:58.365
"No one knows exactly—maybe weeks or months.

73
00:04:59.145 --> 00:05:04.449
After the fires dust from the explosion might have blocked light from reaching Earth's surface.

74
00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:10.153
In the following years, plants, which need light to make food, would have died.

75
00:05:11.694 --> 00:05:14.736
Then plant-eating dinosaurs would have starved and died.

76
00:05:15.284 --> 00:05:18.826
And then the meat-eating dinosaurs would have starved and died too."

77
00:05:18.846 --> 00:05:21.267
"How do we know that?"

78
00:05:21.708 --> 00:05:22.248
Will asked.

79
00:05:23.248 --> 00:05:28.571
"We can guess when species lived based on their fossils and what layer of rock we find those

80
00:05:28.611 --> 00:05:29.352
fossils in.

81
00:05:30.132 --> 00:05:35.455
The species that went extinct don't appear in rocks formed after 65 million years ago."

82
00:05:36.716 --> 00:05:38.757
Will thought about everything QT had said.

83
00:05:38.777 --> 00:05:44.260
"But scientists aren't sure whether the volcanoes or the asteroid caused the dinosaur extinction?"

84
00:05:46.152 --> 00:05:47.873
"It's possible both contributed.

85
00:05:48.353 --> 00:05:51.695
There are other factors and theories too," QT replied.

86
00:05:53.076 --> 00:05:59.119
"For instance, some people think mammals ate so many dinosaur eggs that dinosaurs couldn't survive.

87
00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.001
And we're not sure whether dinosaurs died suddenly.

88
00:06:03.481 --> 00:06:08.164
They could have been dying off gradually before the volcanoes or asteroid became a problem.”

89
00:06:09.625 --> 00:06:12.946
QT paused, and the scenery outside began to transform.

90
00:06:12.966 --> 00:06:15.628
"We've jumped forward just a few years.

91
00:06:16.268 --> 00:06:17.308
See all those animals?

92
00:06:18.649 --> 00:06:24.050
Many mammals, frogs, crocodiles, and even some species of dinosaurs survived the extinction.

93
00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:25.711
But we don't know why."

94
00:06:26.951 --> 00:06:30.972
Will remembered the ferocious-looking Tyrannosaurus at the museum and shuddered.

95
00:06:30.992 --> 00:06:34.413
"Did some dinosaurs survive into modern times?"

96
00:06:36.353 --> 00:06:42.995
"Well, scientists are pretty sure birds evolved from dinosaurs, so technically they are dinosaurs.

97
00:06:43.855 --> 00:06:50.895
And modern crocodiles aren't dinosaurs, but they are very similar to the crocodiles that were alive 65 million

98
00:06:50.915 --> 00:06:52.736
years ago," QT said.

99
00:06:53.476 --> 00:06:55.437
Suddenly something rose out of the water.

100
00:06:55.997 --> 00:06:58.379
Its jaws snapped shut on the tail of the aircraft!

101
00:06:58.399 --> 00:07:05.082
"No!" Will shut his eyes, expecting the crocodile to pull them underwater.

102
00:07:05.543 --> 00:07:07.364
The aircraft shook and then was still.

103
00:07:09.124 --> 00:07:12.746
Will peeked and realized that the bus had jolted to a stop in front of the school.

104
00:07:12.766 --> 00:07:14.227
"Wake up!"

105
00:07:14.828 --> 00:07:15.348
Bobby said.

106
00:07:15.884 --> 00:07:17.447
"I hope you had a nice nap!"

107
00:07:18.649 --> 00:07:21.193
"I had the strangest dream about dinosaurs.

108
00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.438
I don't think I'll ever forget the stuff I learned today!"

109
00:07:25.019 --> 00:07:25.480
Will said.
